      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MINNIE MIA (1) went back last start then worked home in good style to finish 5 metres from the winner in third at Shepparton over 1690m when returning from a break. Sure to enjoy an economical run from this draw. Meets a comparable field and she can go right on with the job. THE PASO DOBLE (5) has been a bit hot and cold and that continued last start when he finished second, beaten 5 metres, in a better performance at Stawell over 2180m. Big chance in a similar race. MAJESTIC PHILLY NZ (2) must be considered after she finished third when resuming over 1609m at Geelong a week-and-a-half ago. HIGH RELIABILITY (3) lines up for the first time. By Aldebaran Eagle and hails from the Brent Murphy stable. Has the benefit of a good draw. Has the right credentials to play a major role.",
